b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for assignment statements (4.2), the for statement with a while element (4.6) and conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), and the message loop and observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: e, of b becomes e. A line 2: f, of d becomes f . b. A line 3: e, of b becomes b + e. A line 4: e, of b becomes e;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P10c. Named quantities b and d, each an integer variable with a Boolean that says whether it has a value. Each stage replaces a value by an assignment, the right side taken at the values before the stage. d becomes f . b is an assignment, computed once, and d keeps that value when b is replaced. Earlier values are not kept;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, e, f, b, d;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ bk, dk;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  bk := dk := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, the stage it poses, and then that stage's constants;
    code := read; k := read;
    i̲f̲ k = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ b becomes e;
      e := read; b := e; bk := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ d becomes f . b;
      f := read; d := f × b; dk := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ b becomes b + e;
      e := read; b := b + e e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ b becomes e;
      e := read; b := e e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: the values b and d have now;
    PRINTTEXT(`[answer]b');
    i̲f̲ bk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` = '); print(b) e̲n̲d̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` has no value');
    PRINTTEXT(`, d');
    i̲f̲ dk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` = '); print(d) e̲n̲d̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` has no value');
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the one value held for each quantity;
    PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`b and d are variables, replaced by assignment, and their earlier values are not kept. No relation is held'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ bk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind b]'); print(b); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ dk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind d]'); print(d); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
